The Clockmaker’s Riddle

In the heart of an ancient city, a reclusive clockmaker named Elias Tock 
left behind a legacy shrouded in enigma. Known for his intricate timepieces, 
Elias was rumored to guard a secret so profound that he encoded it within a 
message only the sharpest minds could unravel. His workshop, now a crumbling
ruin, yielded a single clue: a weathered parchment bearing strange text, 
etched in a cipher that ticks like the hands of a clock.
Our agents recovered the following ciphertext:
pqJ/#{a0Z#qA3t1nnTi1P`+c;DB{J
Whispers among cryptographers suggest Elias wove his obsession with time 
into the very fabric of his cipher. Some say the 
key lies in the rhythm of his craft—a phrase that echoes the 
relentless march of seconds, minutes, and hours for him the time is the key. Others believe it’s 
tied to the tools of his trade, a sequence as vital as the gears he once turned.
Your task is to decode this message and uncover Elias’s secret. The flag awaits within, 
locked in the past, ticking toward revelation. Submit it in the standard format: FLAG{...}.

Hint:

